  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe machine file `assets/machines/fehlmann-picomax55.mch` does not state the travel limits (\"Reference-frame travel limits are unstated\"), the spindle mount, or rigid tapping. Its description also names one source file by its file name; a neutral source note is enough.\n\n## Expected\n\nFrom the machine's operating manual (section 7.1, \"Mechanische Daten\", Picomax 55 CNC 2/3) and the machine owner:\n- Travel: X 500 mm, Y 255 mm, Z (quill, CNC) 147 mm. State them as travel limits, so that CamCraft can refuse a move outside the working range. Choose the zero point of each range from the existing kinematics and say how in the PR.\n- Spindle mount: SF32 (the manual names SF32 as the tool holder).\n- Rigid tapping: yes (the machine owner confirms rigid tapping; the manual lists tapping up to M20 in steel 700 N/mm²).\n- Spindle speed: keep 50 to 9000 min⁻¹. The manual lists 50 to 7100 for the standard spindle; this machine has the 9000 min⁻¹ spindle (machine owner, and the machine parameters).\n- Feed rates stay as they are (they agree with the manual: X/Y 11000, Z 6000 mm/min).\n- Description: replace the parameter file name with a neutral note (\"the machine parameters\").\n\n## Done means\n\n- The machine file states the travel limits, the SF32 mount and rigid tapping.\n- A test pins that a move outside a travel limit is refused by name on this machine (or the existing travel-limit law covers it, with the test named in the PR).\n- The posted output of the Picomax goldens does not change.\n- The description names no parameter file.\n\nEffort: low (one machine file and its tests).\n",
